% Pure idempotent absorption: f(x, x) = x.  Conjecture
% f(a, f(a, a)) = a should reduce in two rewrites under the
% top-down recursive rewriter (inner f(a, a) -> a, then outer
% f(a, a) -> a).  Tests the rewriter's recursion-into-children
% path on a flat-but-non-trivial conjecture.
NAME            idempotent_nested
MODE            PROOF
SORTS           ANY
SIGNATURE       f: ANY ANY -> ANY
                a: -> ANY
ORDERING        LPO
                f > a
VARIABLES       x : ANY
EQUATIONS       f(x, x) = x
CONCLUSION      f(a, f(a, a)) = a
